==Icelandic==

===Etymology===
From {{m|is|ég||I, the personal pronoun}} and {{m|is|heiti||I'm called}}, first person form of {{m|is|heita||to be called, to be named}}. Literally meaning "I am called" or "I am named".

===Phrase===
'''[[ég#Icelandic|ég]] [[heita#Icelandic|heiti]]'''

# [[I]] [[am]]; [[my name is]]
#: '''''Ég heiti''' Ríkharður.''
#:: '''''My name is''' Richard.''
#: '''''Ég heiti''' Braga, [[hvað heitir þú]]?''
#:: '''My name is''' Braga, [[what's your name]]?

====Related terms====
* [[hvað heitir þú]]?, [[hvað heitirðu]]?

